From d4bb50ace9b1032df120aa613318feb8c7984fbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:23:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Look for the iPhone's RemotePairing port again when its port
 breaks the connection

SideStore reaches this iPhone through LocalDevVPN at the port of its
RemotePairing service: 49152, unless it found another one. iOS gives
that service the port it is given as it starts, not always 49152:
another service of the iPhone can hold that one and answer in its
place, then break the connection as soon as SideStore speaks. The
port answers minimuxer's probe, and the connection is reset at once,
which minimuxer gives as invalidVPN. SideStore looked for the
service's port again, through Bonjour, only for noDevice and
notReachable, so such a port kept the sign-in, a renewal and an update
failing within a second, whatever the player did: LocalDevVPN
connected again, the iPhone restarted.

When the port breaks the connection (reset, early end, broken pipe,
refused) or does not answer minimuxer's probe, SideStore now looks for
the service's port again, and goes on with the one it finds. Should
that one answer no better, as the port of another device on the
network would not, it goes back to the port before. The outcome gives
"portLookup": "moved" when it went on with another port, "same" when
Bonjour found the port it used, "notFound" when it found none.

Needs proper testing on an iPhone whose RemotePairing service is not at
49152.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
